# Defaults for nektos/act, so `act` and `make ci-local` agree.
#
# catthehacker's image is the closest freely available stand-in for a
# GitHub-hosted ubuntu-latest runner. The `medium` variant carries the tools
# the workflow actually uses; the `micro` default lacks too much and the
# `large` one is a ~40 GB pull for nothing this repo needs.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

# Every job in ci.yml runs inside its own `container:`, so what the runner
# image provides barely matters -- but act still needs one to host the job.
--container-architecture linux/amd64

# Quieter default; pass -v when a workflow misbehaves.
--rm
